<title>USA: CBOE to list three options August 1, one August 4.</title>
<headline>CBOE to list three options August 1, one August 4.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board Options Exchange said it will begin trading options on three stocks on August 1 and on one other stock on August 4.</p>
<p>The options to be listed on August 1 include McLeodUSA Inc, Mercantile Bankshares Corp and American Depositary Receipts of Rhone-Poulenc SA.</p>
<p>On August 4, the exchange will list options on Patterson Energy Inc.</p>
<p>The following table lists the stocks' ticker symbols, the options' strike prices and expiration months and the designated primary market maker (DPM) or trading crowd.  </p>
<p>Ticker	Strikes	 Expiry	DPM/Trading Crowd</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>MCLD.O	30, 35, 40    Aug, Sep,   Hewlett-Packard</p>
<p>				  Oct, Jan    trading crowd</p>
<p>MRBK.O	25, 30, 35    Aug, Sep,   RMB &amp; Associates</p>
<p>				  Nov, Feb</p>
<p>RP.N	  35, 40, 45    Aug, Sep,   Cohen, Duffy &amp; McGowan</p>
<p>				  Oct, Jan</p>
<p>PTEN.O	25, 30, 35    Aug, Sep,   Honeywell Inc</p>
<p>				  Nov, Feb    trading crowd</p>
<p>((--Chicago derivatives desk, 312 408 8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
